Subject: [PATCH] db: the database password stays out of the controller's log

db_client_t::connect printed the login it was given, user and password ("user:... pass:..."), at
every start of the controller. Its output goes to the controller's log file, which a platform's
log tarballs and log upload may carry off the box. The line stays, with the user; the password
reads <redacted>.
---
diff --git a/src/db/db_client.cpp b/src/db/db_client.cpp
index 229c3052..f752faf5 100644
--- a/src/db/db_client.cpp
+++ b/src/db/db_client.cpp
@@ -167,7 +167,8 @@
      strncpy(password, tmp, sizeof(password) - 1);
      password[sizeof(password) - 1] = '\0';
 
-     printf("%s:%d: user:%s pass:%s\n", __func__, __LINE__, username, password);
+     /* the database password stays out of the log (em_ctrl.txt) */
+     printf("%s:%d: user:%s pass:<redacted>\n", __func__, __LINE__, username);
 
      // Initialize MySQL connection
      m_con = mysql_init(NULL);
